# The cosign module's own convention is to commit cosign.pub and keep only
# cosign.key out of the repo — right for a real project with one shared
# signing identity. This demo has no "team": everyone who runs it signs
# against their own disposable local registry, so the whole key pair is
# generated fresh by `task sign` and none of it belongs in git.
